{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1788686247799,"sessionID":"ses_f89fe2701ffe6lTPBHqSpApZWe","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"read","callID":"chatcmpl-tool-9b6ccf3cd0695273","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"filePath":"/home/kantord/.local/share/toylang-lanes/issue-benchmark-fasta-build/benches/programs/binary-trees.toy"},"output":"<path>/home/kantord/.local/share/toylang-lanes/issue-benchmark-fasta-build/benches/programs/binary-trees.toy</path>\n<type>file</type>\n<content>\n1: enum Tree { Leaf, Node(Vec<Tree>) }\n2: \n3: fn build(depth: Int) -> Tree =\n4:     depth | . == 0 -> Tree.leaf or Tree.node([build(. - 1), build(. - 1)])\n5: \n6: fn count(t: Tree) -> Int =\n7:     t | Leaf -> 1 or Node -> 1 + count(.[0]!) + count(.[1]!)\n8: \n9: count(build(parse(stdin)))\n\n(End of file - total 9 lines)\n</content>","metadata":{"preview":"enum Tree { Leaf, Node(Vec<Tree>) }\n\nfn build(depth: Int) -> Tree =\n    depth | . == 0 -> Tree.leaf or Tree.node([build(. - 1), build(. - 1)])\n\nfn count(t: Tree) -> Int =\n    t | Leaf -> 1 or Node -> 1 + count(.[0]!) + count(.[1]!)\n\ncount(build(parse(stdin)))","truncated":false,"loaded":[],"display":{"type":"file","path":"/home/kantord/.local/share/toylang-lanes/issue-benchmark-fasta-build/benches/programs/binary-trees.toy","text":"enum Tree { Leaf, Node(Vec<Tree>) }\n\nfn build(depth: Int) -> Tree =\n    depth | . == 0 -> Tree.leaf or Tree.node([build(. - 1), build(. - 1)])\n\nfn count(t: Tree) -> Int =\n    t | Leaf -> 1 or Node -> 1 + count(.[0]!) + count(.[1]!)\n\ncount(build(parse(stdin)))","lineStart":1,"lineEnd":9,"totalLines":9,"truncated":false}},"title":"benches/programs/binary-trees.toy","time":{"start":1788686247792,"end":1788686247798}},"metadata":{"openrouter":{"reasoning_details":[{"type":"reasoning.text","text":"The issue `benchmark-fasta-build` isn't a real GitHub issue (invalid format). The board row is `benchmark-fasta-build` in benchmark-plan.md \"Build status\". So I should implement the fasta benchmark in toylang.\n\nLet me look at:\n1. The existing `benches/programs/binary-trees.toy`\n2. The corpus case `tests/corpus/binary_trees_node_count.yaml`\n3. The bench runner `src/bin/bench.rs`\n4. `benches/inputs/binary-trees.txt`\n\nLet me read these.","format":"unknown","index":0}]}},"id":"prt_076022283001T2b5zaOpp5nkVY","sessionID":"ses_f89fe2701ffe6lTPBHqSpApZWe","messageID":"msg_076021355001oqIxvh12vDfOgR"}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1788686248142,"sessionID":"ses_f89fe2701ffe6lTPBHqSpApZWe","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"read","callID":"chatcmpl-tool-a33460d810c65fe8","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"filePath":"/home/kantord/.local/share/toylang-lanes/issue-benchmark-fasta-build/tests/corpus/binary_trees_node_count.yaml"},"output":"<path>/home/kantord/.local/share/toylang-lanes/issue-benchmark-fasta-build/tests/corpus/binary_trees_node_count.yaml</path>\n<type>file</type>\n<content>\n1: # The core of the CLBG binary-trees task (kantord/toylang#106, benchmark suite): build a\n2: # perfect binary tree of a given depth and count its nodes. The recursive self-reference goes\n3: # through `Vec<Tree>` per the enum-recursion rule (docs/reference/types/enum.md), with `node`'s\n4: # Vec always holding exactly two children. This is the correctness fixture for\n5: # benches/programs/binary-trees.toy, at a depth small enough to run fast on every backend; the\n6: # benchmark input under benches/inputs/ uses a larger depth for real timing.\n7: #\n8: # Derived: Computer Language Benchmarks Game binary-trees task,\n9: # https://benchmarksgame-team.pages.debian.net/benchmarksgame/, BSD-3-Clause -- reimplemented\n10: # from the task's plain description (build a tree, count nodes), not copied from any reference\n11: # source.\n12: program: |\n13:   enum Tree { Leaf, Node(Vec<Tree>) }\n14: \n15:   fn build(depth: Int) -> Tree =\n16:       depth | . == 0 -> Tree.leaf or Tree.node([build(. - 1), build(. - 1)])\n17: \n18:   fn count(t: Tree) -> Int =\n19:       t | Leaf -> 1 or Node -> 1 + count(.[0]!) + count(.[1]!)\n20: \n21:   count(build(parse(stdin)))\n22: \n23: input: |\n24:   6\n25: \n26: output: |\n27:   127\n28: \n29: node_types: [application, arith.add, arith.sub, compare.eq, input, int, local, match, pipe, selection.collapse, unwrap, var, variant.payload, variant.unit, vec-literal]\n\n(End of file - total 29 lines)\n</content>","metadata":{"preview":"# The core of the CLBG binary-trees task (kantord/toylang#106, benchmark suite): build a\n# perfect binary tree of a given depth and count its nodes. The recursive self-reference goes\n# through `Vec<Tree>` per the enum-recursion rule (docs/reference/types/enum.md), with `node`'s\n# Vec always holding exactly two children. This is the correctness fixture for\n# benches/programs/binary-trees.toy, at a depth small enough to run fast on every backend; the\n# benchmark input under benches/inputs/ uses a larger depth for real timing.\n#\n# Derived: Computer Language Benchmarks Game binary-trees task,\n# https://benchmarksgame-team.pages.debian.net/benchmarksgame/, BSD-3-Clause -- reimplemented\n# from the task's plain description (build a tree, count nodes), not copied from any reference\n# source.\nprogram: |\n  enum Tree { Leaf, Node(Vec<Tree>) }\n\n  fn build(depth: Int) -> Tree =\n      depth | . == 0 -> Tree.leaf or Tree.node([build(. - 1), build(. - 1)])\n\n  fn count(t: Tree) -> Int =\n      t | Leaf -> 1 or Node -> 1 + count(.[0]!) + count(.[1]!)\n","truncated":false,"loaded":[],"display":{"type":"file","path":"/home/kantord/.local/share/toylang-lanes/issue-benchmark-fasta-build/tests/corpus/binary_trees_node_count.yaml","text":"# The core of the CLBG binary-trees task (kantord/toylang#106, benchmark suite): build a\n# perfect binary tree of a given depth and count its nodes. The recursive self-reference goes\n# through `Vec<Tree>` per the enum-recursion rule (docs/reference/types/enum.md), with `node`'s\n# Vec always holding exactly two children. This is the correctness fixture for\n# benches/programs/binary-trees.toy, at a depth small enough to run fast on every backend; the\n# benchmark input under benches/inputs/ uses a larger depth for real timing.\n#\n# Derived: Computer Language Benchmarks Game binary-trees task,\n# https://benchmarksgame-team.pages.debian.net/benchmarksgame/, BSD-3-Clause -- reimplemented\n# from the task's plain description (build a tree, count nodes), not copied from any reference\n# source.\nprogram: |\n  enum Tree { Leaf, Node(Vec<Tree>) }\n\n  fn build(depth: Int) -> Tree =\n      depth | . == 0 -> Tree.leaf or Tree.node([build(. - 1), build(. - 1)])\n\n  fn count(t: Tree) -> Int =\n      t | Leaf -> 1 or Node -> 1 + count(.[0]!) + count(.[1]!)\n\n  count(build(parse(stdin)))\n\ninput: |\n  6\n\noutput: |\n  127\n\nnode_types: [application, arith.add, arith.sub, compare.eq, input, int, local, match, pipe, selection.collapse, unwrap, var, variant.payload, variant.unit, vec-literal]","lineStart":1,"lineEnd":29,"totalLines":29,"truncated":false}},"title":"tests/corpus/binary_trees_node_count.yaml","time":{"start":1788686248131,"end":1788686248140}},"id":"prt_0760227720010GDwZmDb1azK0z","sessionID":"ses_f89fe2701ffe6lTPBHqSpApZWe","messageID":"msg_076021355001oqIxvh12vDfOgR"}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1788686248455,"sessionID":"ses_f89fe2701ffe6lTPBHqSpApZWe","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"read","callID":"chatcmpl-tool-a1731c6f5cd26ae0","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"filePath":"/home/kantord/.local/share/toylang-lanes/issue-benchmark-fasta-build/benches/inputs/binary-trees.txt"},"output":"<path>/home/kantord/.local/share/toylang-lanes/issue-benchmark-fasta-build/benches/inputs/binary-trees.txt</path>\n<type>file</type>\n<content>\n1: 14\n\n(End of file - total 1 lines)\n</content>","metadata":{"preview":"14","truncated":false,"loaded":[],"display":{"type":"file","path":"/home/kantord/.local/share/toylang-lanes/issue-benchmark-fasta-build/benches/inputs/binary-trees.txt","text":"14","lineStart":1,"lineEnd":1,"totalLines":1,"truncated":false}},"title":"benches/inputs/binary-trees.txt","time":{"start":1788686248445,"end":1788686248452}},"id":"prt_0760228c4001TQv1ijCBa37b81","sessionID":"ses_f89fe2701ffe6lTPBHqSpApZWe","messageID":"msg_076021355001oqIxvh12vDfOgR"}}
