{"type":"step_start","timestamp":1788686254916,"sessionID":"ses_f89fe2701ffe6lTPBHqSpApZWe","part":{"id":"prt_07602433e001e8rHpghaECzqmn","messageID":"msg_076022a1f001Fzh9Z88I6Irftc","sessionID":"ses_f89fe2701ffe6lTPBHqSpApZWe","snapshot":"e455b591a29bff5c36ed2ab3c7c0219ec29ad191","type":"step-start"}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1788686255576,"sessionID":"ses_f89fe2701ffe6lTPBHqSpApZWe","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"read","callID":"chatcmpl-tool-823939513f399253","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"filePath":"/home/kantord/.local/share/toylang-lanes/issue-benchmark-fasta-build/src/bin/bench.rs"},"output":"<path>/home/kantord/.local/share/toylang-lanes/issue-benchmark-fasta-build/src/bin/bench.rs</path>\n<type>file</type>\n<content>\n1: //! The benchmark harness: compiles a `benches/programs/<name>.toy` benchmark once, prepares one\n2: //! runnable command per backend -- building Go, Rust, and Native ahead of time and retargeting\n3: //! Lua at the system interpreter, since hyperfine can only time a real subprocess -- and drives\n4: //! `hyperfine` over all of them. Design: plans/benchmark-plan.md and plans/benchmark-tooling-\n5: //! spike.md.\n6: //!\n7: //! Scope today: a benchmark reads at most one `Int` value from stdin, or nothing. That is every\n8: //! benchmark this harness runs so far (see plans/benchmark-plan.md's note on why the CLBG\n9: //! string-processing tasks are not there yet); a benchmark needing a richer input type, or\n10: //! `inputs`/`lines`, needs this harness extended first, most of all the Lua backend's `t_input`\n11: //! injection below, which assumes an Int.\n12: \n13: use std::path::Path;\n14: use std::process::Command;\n15: \n16: use anyhow::{Context, Result, bail};\n17: use toylang::Backend;\n18: \n19: fn main() -> Result<()> {\n20:     let name = std::env::args()\n21:         .nth(1)\n22:         .context(\"usage: bench <name> (a file under benches/programs/)\")?;\n23: \n24:     let src_path = format!(\"benches/programs/{name}.toy\");\n25:     let source =\n26:         std::fs::read_to_string(&src_path).with_context(|| format!(\"could not read {src_path}\"))?;\n27:     let program = toylang::compile(&source).map_err(|e| anyhow::anyhow!(\"{src_path}: {e}\"))?;\n28: \n29:     let input_path = format!(\"benches/inputs/{name}.txt\");\n30:     let input = match std::fs::read_to_string(&input_path) {\n31:         Ok(text) => Some(text.trim().parse::<i64>().with_context(|| {\n32:             format!(\"{input_path}: today's harness only feeds a single Int input\")\n33:         })?),\n34:         Err(e) if e.kind() == std::io::ErrorKind::NotFound => None,\n35:         Err(e) => return Err(e).context(input_path),\n36:     };\n37: \n38:     let work = tempfile::tempdir()?;\n39:     let mut names = Vec::new();\n40:     let mut commands = Vec::new();\n41:     for backend in Backend::ALL {\n42:         match prepare(backend, &program, work.path(), input) {\n43:             Ok(cmd) => {\n44:                 names.push(backend.name().to_string());\n45:                 commands.push(cmd);\n46:             }\n47:             Err(e) => eprintln!(\"bench: skipping {}: {e:#}\", backend.name()),\n48:         }\n49:     }\n50:     if commands.is_empty() {\n51:         bail!(\"no backend could be prepared for {name}\");\n52:     }\n53: \n54:     std::fs::create_dir_all(\"benches/results\")?;\n55:     let mut hyperfine = Command::new(\"hyperfine\");\n56:     hyperfine.arg(\"--shell=none\").arg(\"--warmup\").arg(\"3\");\n57:     if let Some(_n) = input {\n58:         hyperfine.arg(\"--input\").arg(&input_path);\n59:     }\n60:     for (name, cmd) in names.iter().zip(&commands) {\n61:         hyperfine.arg(\"--command-name\").arg(name).arg(cmd);\n62:     }\n63:     hyperfine\n64:         .arg(\"--export-markdown\")\n65:         .arg(format!(\"benches/results/{name}.md\"))\n66:         .arg(\"--export-json\")\n67:         .arg(format!(\"benches/results/{name}.json\"));\n68: \n69:     let status = hyperfine.status().context(\"could not run `hyperfine`\")?;\n70:     if !status.success() {\n71:         bail!(\"hyperfine failed: {status}\");\n72:     }\n73:     Ok(())\n74: }\n75: \n76: /// Builds (where a build step exists) and returns the shell-none command line hyperfine should\n77: /// time for `backend`, as one argv-shaped string. Compiling and, for Go, linking happen here,\n78: /// outside anything hyperfine measures -- the whole reason `run_go` and a bare `emit` are not\n79: /// reused as-is (plans/benchmark-tooling-spike.md).\n80: fn prepare(\n81:     backend: Backend,\n82:     program: &toylang::tir::Program,\n83:     work: &Path,\n84:     input: Option<i64>,\n85: ) -> Result<String> {\n86:     match backend {\n87:         Backend::Lua => {\n88:             let mut source = String::new();\n89:             if let Some(n) = input {\n90:                 // The subprocess has no host setting the `t_input` global the way the embedded\n91:                 // interpreter does (`run_lua` in src/lib.rs) -- so it is set in the script text\n92:                 // itself before the emitted body, the same variable name emit_lua::INPUT names.\n93:                 source.push_str(&format!(\"t_input = {n}\\n\"));\n94:             }\n95:             source.push_str(&backend.emit(program).map_err(anyhow::Error::msg)?);\n96:             let path = work.join(\"binary.lua\");\n97:             std::fs::write(&path, source)?;\n98:             Ok(format!(\"lua5.4 {}\", path.display()))\n99:         }\n100:         Backend::Js => {\n101:             let path = work.join(\"binary.js\");\n102:             std::fs::write(&path, backend.emit(program).map_err(anyhow::Error::msg)?)?;\n103:             Ok(format!(\"node {}\", path.display()))\n104:         }\n105:         Backend::Py => {\n106:             let path = work.join(\"binary.py\");\n107:             std::fs::write(&path, backend.emit(program).map_err(anyhow::Error::msg)?)?;\n108:             Ok(format!(\"python3 {}\", path.display()))\n109:         }\n110:         Backend::Jq => {\n111:             let filter = backend.emit(program).map_err(anyhow::Error::msg)?;\n112:             let mut argv = vec![\n113:                 \"jq\".to_string(),\n114:                 \"--unbuffered\".to_string(),\n115:                 \"-c\".to_string(),\n116:             ];\n117:             if input.is_none() {\n118:                 argv.push(\"-n\".to_string());\n119:             }\n120:             argv.push(format!(\"'{filter}'\"));\n121:             Ok(argv.join(\" \"))\n122:         }\n123:         Backend::Go => {\n124:             let dir = work.join(\"go\");\n125:             std::fs::create_dir_all(&dir)?;\n126:             let src = dir.join(\"main.go\");\n127:             std::fs::write(&src, backend.emit(program).map_err(anyhow::Error::msg)?)?;\n128:             let bin = dir.join(\"binary\");\n129:             let status = Command::new(\"go\")\n130:                 .arg(\"build\")\n131:                 .arg(\"-o\")\n132:                 .arg(&bin)\n133:                 .arg(&src)\n134:                 .status()\n135:                 .context(\"could not run `go build`\")?;\n136:             if !status.success() {\n137:                 bail!(\"go build failed: {status}\");\n138:             }\n139:             Ok(bin.display().to_string())\n140:         }\n141:         Backend::Native => {\n142:             let exe = work.join(\"binary-native\");\n143:             toylang::link(program, &exe)?;\n144:             Ok(exe.display().to_string())\n145:         }\n146:         Backend::Rust => {\n147:             let exe = work.join(\"binary-rust\");\n148:             let source = backend.emit(program).map_err(anyhow::Error::msg)?;\n149:             toylang::link_rust(&source, &exe)?;\n150:             Ok(exe.display().to_string())\n151:         }\n152:     }\n153: }\n\n(End of file - total 153 lines)\n</content>","metadata":{"preview":"//! The benchmark harness: compiles a `benches/programs/<name>.toy` benchmark once, prepares one\n//! runnable command per backend -- building Go, Rust, and Native ahead of time and retargeting\n//! Lua at the system interpreter, since hyperfine can only time a real subprocess -- and drives\n//! `hyperfine` over all of them. Design: plans/benchmark-plan.md and plans/benchmark-tooling-\n//! spike.md.\n//!\n//! Scope today: a benchmark reads at most one `Int` value from stdin, or nothing. That is every\n//! benchmark this harness runs so far (see plans/benchmark-plan.md's note on why the CLBG\n//! string-processing tasks are not there yet); a benchmark needing a richer input type, or\n//! `inputs`/`lines`, needs this harness extended first, most of all the Lua backend's `t_input`\n//! injection below, which assumes an Int.\n\nuse std::path::Path;\nuse std::process::Command;\n\nuse anyhow::{Context, Result, bail};\nuse toylang::Backend;\n\nfn main() -> Result<()> {\n    let name = std::env::args()","truncated":false,"loaded":[],"display":{"type":"file","path":"/home/kantord/.local/share/toylang-lanes/issue-benchmark-fasta-build/src/bin/bench.rs","text":"//! The benchmark harness: compiles a `benches/programs/<name>.toy` benchmark once, prepares one\n//! runnable command per backend -- building Go, Rust, and Native ahead of time and retargeting\n//! Lua at the system interpreter, since hyperfine can only time a real subprocess -- and drives\n//! `hyperfine` over all of them. Design: plans/benchmark-plan.md and plans/benchmark-tooling-\n//! spike.md.\n//!\n//! Scope today: a benchmark reads at most one `Int` value from stdin, or nothing. That is every\n//! benchmark this harness runs so far (see plans/benchmark-plan.md's note on why the CLBG\n//! string-processing tasks are not there yet); a benchmark needing a richer input type, or\n//! `inputs`/`lines`, needs this harness extended first, most of all the Lua backend's `t_input`\n//! injection below, which assumes an Int.\n\nuse std::path::Path;\nuse std::process::Command;\n\nuse anyhow::{Context, Result, bail};\nuse toylang::Backend;\n\nfn main() -> Result<()> {\n    let name = std::env::args()\n        .nth(1)\n        .context(\"usage: bench <name> (a file under benches/programs/)\")?;\n\n    let src_path = format!(\"benches/programs/{name}.toy\");\n    let source =\n        std::fs::read_to_string(&src_path).with_context(|| format!(\"could not read {src_path}\"))?;\n    let program = toylang::compile(&source).map_err(|e| anyhow::anyhow!(\"{src_path}: {e}\"))?;\n\n    let input_path = format!(\"benches/inputs/{name}.txt\");\n    let input = match std::fs::read_to_string(&input_path) {\n        Ok(text) => Some(text.trim().parse::<i64>().with_context(|| {\n            format!(\"{input_path}: today's harness only feeds a single Int input\")\n        })?),\n        Err(e) if e.kind() == std::io::ErrorKind::NotFound => None,\n        Err(e) => return Err(e).context(input_path),\n    };\n\n    let work = tempfile::tempdir()?;\n    let mut names = Vec::new();\n    let mut commands = Vec::new();\n    for backend in Backend::ALL {\n        match prepare(backend, &program, work.path(), input) {\n            Ok(cmd) => {\n                names.push(backend.name().to_string());\n                commands.push(cmd);\n            }\n            Err(e) => eprintln!(\"bench: skipping {}: {e:#}\", backend.name()),\n        }\n    }\n    if commands.is_empty() {\n        bail!(\"no backend could be prepared for {name}\");\n    }\n\n    std::fs::create_dir_all(\"benches/results\")?;\n    let mut hyperfine = Command::new(\"hyperfine\");\n    hyperfine.arg(\"--shell=none\").arg(\"--warmup\").arg(\"3\");\n    if let Some(_n) = input {\n        hyperfine.arg(\"--input\").arg(&input_path);\n    }\n    for (name, cmd) in names.iter().zip(&commands) {\n        hyperfine.arg(\"--command-name\").arg(name).arg(cmd);\n    }\n    hyperfine\n        .arg(\"--export-markdown\")\n        .arg(format!(\"benches/results/{name}.md\"))\n        .arg(\"--export-json\")\n        .arg(format!(\"benches/results/{name}.json\"));\n\n    let status = hyperfine.status().context(\"could not run `hyperfine`\")?;\n    if !status.success() {\n        bail!(\"hyperfine failed: {status}\");\n    }\n    Ok(())\n}\n\n/// Builds (where a build step exists) and returns the shell-none command line hyperfine should\n/// time for `backend`, as one argv-shaped string. Compiling and, for Go, linking happen here,\n/// outside anything hyperfine measures -- the whole reason `run_go` and a bare `emit` are not\n/// reused as-is (plans/benchmark-tooling-spike.md).\nfn prepare(\n    backend: Backend,\n    program: &toylang::tir::Program,\n    work: &Path,\n    input: Option<i64>,\n) -> Result<String> {\n    match backend {\n        Backend::Lua => {\n            let mut source = String::new();\n            if let Some(n) = input {\n                // The subprocess has no host setting the `t_input` global the way the embedded\n                // interpreter does (`run_lua` in src/lib.rs) -- so it is set in the script text\n                // itself before the emitted body, the same variable name emit_lua::INPUT names.\n                source.push_str(&format!(\"t_input = {n}\\n\"));\n            }\n            source.push_str(&backend.emit(program).map_err(anyhow::Error::msg)?);\n            let path = work.join(\"binary.lua\");\n            std::fs::write(&path, source)?;\n            Ok(format!(\"lua5.4 {}\", path.display()))\n        }\n        Backend::Js => {\n            let path = work.join(\"binary.js\");\n            std::fs::write(&path, backend.emit(program).map_err(anyhow::Error::msg)?)?;\n            Ok(format!(\"node {}\", path.display()))\n        }\n        Backend::Py => {\n            let path = work.join(\"binary.py\");\n            std::fs::write(&path, backend.emit(program).map_err(anyhow::Error::msg)?)?;\n            Ok(format!(\"python3 {}\", path.display()))\n        }\n        Backend::Jq => {\n            let filter = backend.emit(program).map_err(anyhow::Error::msg)?;\n            let mut argv = vec![\n                \"jq\".to_string(),\n                \"--unbuffered\".to_string(),\n                \"-c\".to_string(),\n            ];\n            if input.is_none() {\n                argv.push(\"-n\".to_string());\n            }\n            argv.push(format!(\"'{filter}'\"));\n            Ok(argv.join(\" \"))\n        }\n        Backend::Go => {\n            let dir = work.join(\"go\");\n            std::fs::create_dir_all(&dir)?;\n            let src = dir.join(\"main.go\");\n            std::fs::write(&src, backend.emit(program).map_err(anyhow::Error::msg)?)?;\n            let bin = dir.join(\"binary\");\n            let status = Command::new(\"go\")\n                .arg(\"build\")\n                .arg(\"-o\")\n                .arg(&bin)\n                .arg(&src)\n                .status()\n                .context(\"could not run `go build`\")?;\n            if !status.success() {\n                bail!(\"go build failed: {status}\");\n            }\n            Ok(bin.display().to_string())\n        }\n        Backend::Native => {\n            let exe = work.join(\"binary-native\");\n            toylang::link(program, &exe)?;\n            Ok(exe.display().to_string())\n        }\n        Backend::Rust => {\n            let exe = work.join(\"binary-rust\");\n            let source = backend.emit(program).map_err(anyhow::Error::msg)?;\n            toylang::link_rust(&source, &exe)?;\n            Ok(exe.display().to_string())\n        }\n    }\n}","lineStart":1,"lineEnd":153,"totalLines":153,"truncated":false}},"title":"src/bin/bench.rs","time":{"start":1788686255566,"end":1788686255574}},"metadata":{"openrouter":{"reasoning_details":[{"type":"reasoning.text","text":"Now let me look at the bench runner and the justfile, and understand how benches/inputs is fed.","format":"unknown","index":0}]}},"id":"prt_0760244ad001rO22Aw1XxhOk05","sessionID":"ses_f89fe2701ffe6lTPBHqSpApZWe","messageID":"msg_076022a1f001Fzh9Z88I6Irftc"}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1788686256025,"sessionID":"ses_f89fe2701ffe6lTPBHqSpApZWe","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"read","callID":"chatcmpl-tool-b7603d021f6e031b","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"filePath":"/home/kantord/.local/share/toylang-lanes/issue-benchmark-fasta-build/justfile"},"output":"<path>/home/kantord/.local/share/toylang-lanes/issue-benchmark-fasta-build/justfile</path>\n<type>file</type>\n<content>\n1: # List available recipes.\n2: default:\n3:     @just --list\n4: \n5: # The final gate: the full test suite. Landing requires this green.\n6: test:\n7:     cargo nextest run\n8: \n9: # The fast inner loop: skips the docs mega-test, the suite's ~137s long pole. Gate on `just test`.\n10: check:\n11:     cargo nextest run -E 'not test(every_fragment_is_a_real_program)'\n12: \n13: # Opt-in: run the skipped Euler 8/11/13/18 programs against real puzzle data in DIR, outside\n14: # `just test`. DIR holds your own copies of the raw data texts; fails loudly, never skips.\n15: euler-data DIR:\n16:     EULER_DATA={{DIR}} cargo nextest run --run-ignored ignored-only -E 'test(euler_real_data)'\n17: \n18: # Re-run the slow-fragment tier: the same suite, but `slow` fragments are executed on every\n19: # backend rather than only type-checked and emitted. The tier exists so `just test` stays fast;\n20: # this is where the deferred execution claim is re-verified.\n21: slow-test:\n22:     TOYLANG_SLOW=1 cargo nextest run\n23: \n24: # Run clippy with the repo's lint set, the same surface the Stop hook checks.\n25: clippy:\n26:     cargo clippy --workspace --all-targets\n27: \n28: # Time one benchmark (a name under benches/programs/) across every backend with hyperfine.\n29: # Design: plans/benchmark-plan.md. Results land in benches/results/<name>.{md,json}.\n30: bench NAME:\n31:     cargo run -q --bin bench -- {{NAME}}\n32: \n33: # Formatter check over every .toy file from the repo root down (exit 1 on drift).\n34: fmt:\n35:     cargo run -q -- fmt\n36: \n37: # Rewrite drifted files in place (same exit code as the check).\n38: fmt-write:\n39:     cargo run -q -- fmt --write\n40: \n41: # The repo's mechanical checks, the same surface the Stop hook runs.\n42: checks:\n43:     bash .claude/checks/run.sh\n44: \n45: # The autonomous drive loop: a tick every 600s, live colorized output, Ctrl-C to stop. Run ONE.\n46: drive:\n47:     .claude/scripts/drive-loop.sh\n48: \n49: # Fire one coordinator tick right now (zero tokens if there is nothing to do).\n50: tick:\n51:     .claude/scripts/drive-tick.sh\n52: \n53: # Watch the current coordinator tick live (detaches with Ctrl-C, tick untouched).\n54: peek:\n55:     .claude/scripts/tick-peek.sh\n\n(End of file - total 55 lines)\n</content>","metadata":{"preview":"# List available recipes.\ndefault:\n    @just --list\n\n# The final gate: the full test suite. Landing requires this green.\ntest:\n    cargo nextest run\n\n# The fast inner loop: skips the docs mega-test, the suite's ~137s long pole. Gate on `just test`.\ncheck:\n    cargo nextest run -E 'not test(every_fragment_is_a_real_program)'\n\n# Opt-in: run the skipped Euler 8/11/13/18 programs against real puzzle data in DIR, outside\n# `just test`. DIR holds your own copies of the raw data texts; fails loudly, never skips.\neuler-data DIR:\n    EULER_DATA={{DIR}} cargo nextest run --run-ignored ignored-only -E 'test(euler_real_data)'\n\n# Re-run the slow-fragment tier: the same suite, but `slow` fragments are executed on every\n# backend rather than only type-checked and emitted. The tier exists so `just test` stays fast;\n# this is where the deferred execution claim is re-verified.","truncated":false,"loaded":[],"display":{"type":"file","path":"/home/kantord/.local/share/toylang-lanes/issue-benchmark-fasta-build/justfile","text":"# List available recipes.\ndefault:\n    @just --list\n\n# The final gate: the full test suite. Landing requires this green.\ntest:\n    cargo nextest run\n\n# The fast inner loop: skips the docs mega-test, the suite's ~137s long pole. Gate on `just test`.\ncheck:\n    cargo nextest run -E 'not test(every_fragment_is_a_real_program)'\n\n# Opt-in: run the skipped Euler 8/11/13/18 programs against real puzzle data in DIR, outside\n# `just test`. DIR holds your own copies of the raw data texts; fails loudly, never skips.\neuler-data DIR:\n    EULER_DATA={{DIR}} cargo nextest run --run-ignored ignored-only -E 'test(euler_real_data)'\n\n# Re-run the slow-fragment tier: the same suite, but `slow` fragments are executed on every\n# backend rather than only type-checked and emitted. The tier exists so `just test` stays fast;\n# this is where the deferred execution claim is re-verified.\nslow-test:\n    TOYLANG_SLOW=1 cargo nextest run\n\n# Run clippy with the repo's lint set, the same surface the Stop hook checks.\nclippy:\n    cargo clippy --workspace --all-targets\n\n# Time one benchmark (a name under benches/programs/) across every backend with hyperfine.\n# Design: plans/benchmark-plan.md. Results land in benches/results/<name>.{md,json}.\nbench NAME:\n    cargo run -q --bin bench -- {{NAME}}\n\n# Formatter check over every .toy file from the repo root down (exit 1 on drift).\nfmt:\n    cargo run -q -- fmt\n\n# Rewrite drifted files in place (same exit code as the check).\nfmt-write:\n    cargo run -q -- fmt --write\n\n# The repo's mechanical checks, the same surface the Stop hook runs.\nchecks:\n    bash .claude/checks/run.sh\n\n# The autonomous drive loop: a tick every 600s, live colorized output, Ctrl-C to stop. Run ONE.\ndrive:\n    .claude/scripts/drive-loop.sh\n\n# Fire one coordinator tick right now (zero tokens if there is nothing to do).\ntick:\n    .claude/scripts/drive-tick.sh\n\n# Watch the current coordinator tick live (detaches with Ctrl-C, tick untouched).\npeek:\n    .claude/scripts/tick-peek.sh","lineStart":1,"lineEnd":55,"totalLines":55,"truncated":false}},"title":"justfile","time":{"start":1788686256015,"end":1788686256023}},"id":"prt_0760245d2001Prx